    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument",
    "type_designations": ["ZP900 Series", "BSQ Series"],
    "description": "Family of Class III, mains, DC or battery-powered, self-indicating non-automatic weighing instruments (also usable as postal scales), built from Avery Weigh-Tronix BSQ Series digital bases (two-part cast aluminium painted enclosure, load bridge, stainless steel or aluminium weighing pan, digital load cell assembly type LP FPGA QDT, adjustable feet, level indicator) connected to a ZP900 series indicator and optionally a ZP900 series remote display. May be used for direct sales to the public. Devices: initial zero setting (≤ 4% Max), semi-automatic zero setting (≤ 4% Max), zero tracking (≤ 4% Max), single or multi-range operation (maximum of 3 partial ranges), determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, checking of display, gross/zero/motion/Ethernet/battery indicators, range-in-use indicators (multi-range variant). Sealing: jumper on ZP900 indicator main board, or software sealing via non-editable CALIB and CONFIG counters with password-protected access, or hardware sealing with destructible paper seal."
